                <pb facs="0646" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4164 Suppl.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-16T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>14. Department’s telegram No. 12, February 1, 5 p.m. If Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs has not yet taken occasion to resolve the ambiguity as to Japanese
                    Government’s attitude towards consortium loan to China you will please consult
                    with British Ambassador and take early opportunity to see Minister and inquire
                    as to Japanese Government’s position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
